  "term": "coronary heart disease",
  "definition": "Coronary heart disease is a group of heart conditions in which the coronary arteries become narrowed or blocked, usually because of atherosclerosis. It includes problems such as myocardial infarction, angina pectoris, and coronary artery disease, and is a major cause of illness and death.",
